      "role": "user",
      "content": "The 60/40 weighting seems pretty aggressive. Usually, when we present to the council, they expecting a more conservative approach where current market comps are the primary driver, especially since the district hasn't seen any major activity yet. If we lead with a model that's mostly based on projections, they might call it speculative and reject the bond entirely. \n\nIs there any way to adjust the weighting or add a secondary \"baseline\" valuation that relies more heavily on the actual transaction data? I want to make sure we have a version of this report that feels grounded enough to pass their scrutiny, even if the number is a bit lower.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
